  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Big coast to coast – counter-attack via jokers",
  "description": "Split the players into four teams. Two teams play 3v3 with goalkeepers on a pitch of about 40 × 20 metres, and the other two teams are jokers in passing zones along the boards – one joker team in each half (marked J). Each team's jokers stand in the half that team defends.\n\nOne team attacks. When the defending team wins the ball, it must first pass to one of its jokers, and from there it launches a fast counter-attack towards the other goal. The ball stays in play until the defenders have found a joker. Each team plays one attack and one defence, then the teams switch – when the ball goes over the boards or into the goal. Rotate the playing teams and the joker teams too. Goalkeepers are not drawn.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "As soon as you win the ball: look up and find the nearest joker."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Players without the ball run straight forward towards the far goal – not sideways."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Pass in front of the runner so they can take the ball at full speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Finish quickly, before the opponents are back in defence."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "difficulty": 3,
